From 07326c5dfef95f2dbb421d42c8d059761b255f1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:44:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] One action clip gives way to the next over a crossfade, not a
 cut

A clip asked for while another plays swapped nodes at once: the new clip's node took the whole
blend in the frame the old one's was stopped, and the pose jumped between them. On a jump clip
followed by a landing clip the legs snapped from the jump's last pose into the landing's first
(Corey's review: "the legs start to clip and do weird things when he goes to land"). The outgoing
nodes now fade out over 0.12 s (`CROSS_FADE`), each kept on the clip with its weight at the swap
and ramped to nothing before it's stopped, and the automatic full/upper switch as the body starts
or stops moving crossfades the same way instead of stopping the node it leaves. A clip's own fade
in at its start and fade out at its end are as they were.
---
 .../benilla-app/src/creature_anim/action.rs   | 136 ++++++++++++++----
 crates/benilla-ui/src/action_combat.rs        |   3 +
 2 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

